  <h2>About this site</h2>
  <p>AdnanSiddiqui.com is a technical publication. Articles are written in a fixed format: the problem, a simple explanation, a diagram, what has been seen in production, the repo files, and the sources.</p>
  <p>Azure facts are checked against Microsoft Learn before an article is published. Examples use made-up organizations, never real company names. This is a personal blog: opinions are my own and the site is not affiliated with Microsoft.</p>
  <h2>Where to start</h2>
  <p><a href="/start-here/">Start here</a> explains how the site is organized. The <a href="/azure-landing-zone/">Azure Landing Zone series</a> is the first full series.</p>
  <h2>About the repository</h2>
  <p>The <a href="{{ site.repo }}">Azure Landing Zone repository</a> lets you learn, build and operate an Azure landing zone with Terraform. It covers the Cloud Adoption Framework design areas, Corp and Online archetypes, a policy model, labs and day-2 operations.</p>
  <p>It is an independent learning repository. Its Terraform checks run in public GitHub Actions, and the <a href="{{ site.repo }}/blob/main/docs/03-implementation/release-evidence.md">release evidence page</a> says what those checks do and do not prove.</p>
